is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: dns_server
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Internal DNS (BIND/named) on dns_server. Clients can reach the web servers by IP and HTTP is listening on all four servers, but two hostnames no longer resolve.

Mechanism: Name resolution is failing for the older hostnames, so browsers can’t translate those names to IPs and the sites “vanish.” On dns_server, BIND is authoritative only for the “local” zone and recursion is disabled. The zone file (/etc/bind/db.local) contains A records for web0.local → 10.200.0.3, web1.local → 10.200.0.4, web2.local → 10.200.0.5, web3.local → 10.200.0.6. It does not contain entries for web_server_0.local or web_server_1.local. Lookups for these names return NXDOMAIN/REFUSED, while web0.local/web1.local resolve
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=34
